<article class="env-lemma" id="C211">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/C211">Lemma <span data-tag="C211">5.1.4.6</span>.</a> Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a functor between $\infty $-categories which exhibits $\calD $ as an idempotent completion of $\calC $. Then $f$ is cofinal. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Theorem <a href="/tag/974D" data-tag="974D">4.1.3.1</a>, it suffices to prove that for every object $D \in \calD $, simplicial set $\calC \times _{\calD } \calD _{D/}$ is weakly contractible. Lemma <a href="/tag/5851" data-tag="5851">5.1.4.4</a> asserts that $f_{D/}$ is also an idempotent completion, and Lemma <a href="/tag/B0F5" data-tag="B0F5">5.1.4.5</a> completes the proof. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>